WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.841 --> 00:00:03.524
A room full of boys.

00:00:03.548 --> 00:00:07.681
A girl child, hardly nine
or ten years old,

00:00:07.705 --> 00:00:12.410
she is sitting in the center
of the room, surrounded by books.

00:00:13.141 --> 00:00:15.696
She is the only girl among boys,

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:20.856
and is barely missing
her female cousins and friends,

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:25.460
who are inside the home
instead of the school,

00:00:25.767 --> 00:00:32.128
because they are not allowed
to get an education alongside boys.

00:00:32.757 --> 00:00:38.176
There isn't a single functional
girls' school in her village.

00:00:38.732 --> 00:00:42.678
She was born in a Baloch
conservative tribe,

00:00:42.702 --> 00:00:47.545
where women and girls
are a matter of honor.

00:00:48.764 --> 00:00:50.863
She is the eldest in her family,

00:00:50.887 --> 00:00:56.331
and when she was about to be born,
her parents wanted a baby boy.

00:00:56.355 --> 00:00:59.581
But they had bad luck;
a baby girl arrived.

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:06.164
It was customary in her family
to keep girls inside the homes.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:10.560
But her uncle, who was
a university graduate,

00:01:10.966 --> 00:01:15.617
he wanted to give her
an opportunity to see the world,

00:01:15.641 --> 00:01:17.931
to be part of the society.

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:24.244
Luckily, she has a name
that can be used for both men and women.

00:01:24.268 --> 00:01:28.776
So he saw a chance
to change her course of life.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:32.190
So he decided to raise her as a boy.

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:34.403
At three months old,

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:39.926
she went from being
a baby girl, to baby boy.

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:42.502
She is given a boy's getup.

00:01:42.526 --> 00:01:45.323
She is allowed to go outside

00:01:45.347 --> 00:01:47.676
and get an education alongside boys.

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:49.891
She is free, she is confident.

00:01:51.506 --> 00:01:57.674
She observes, she notes
small, everyday injustices

00:01:57.698 --> 00:02:01.603
faced by women and girls in her village.

00:02:02.212 --> 00:02:05.045
When newspapers arrive at her home,

00:02:05.069 --> 00:02:11.497
she watches as it passes
from the eldest man to the youngest man.

00:02:12.395 --> 00:02:17.229
By the time women get hold of the paper,

00:02:17.253 --> 00:02:18.990
it is old news.

00:02:19.796 --> 00:02:23.264
She completes her eighth-grade year.

00:02:23.733 --> 00:02:26.311
Now fear starts to come in.

00:02:26.693 --> 00:02:30.321
This will be the end of her education,

00:02:30.345 --> 00:02:35.029
because the only option
for high school for further study

00:02:35.053 --> 00:02:36.877
is five kilometers away.

00:02:37.458 --> 00:02:40.878
Boys have bicycles, they are free.

00:02:41.303 --> 00:02:42.670
But she knows

00:02:42.694 --> 00:02:48.531
her father will not allow
her to travel on her own,

00:02:48.555 --> 00:02:51.450
even if she were posing as a boy.

00:02:53.163 --> 00:02:55.686
"I can't let you do that.

00:02:56.385 --> 00:03:00.194
And I don't have the time
to walk you there and back.

00:03:00.687 --> 00:03:03.672
Sorry, it is impossible."

00:03:03.696 --> 00:03:05.093
She gets very upset.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:08.376
But a miracle happened.

00:03:09.154 --> 00:03:12.836
A long-distance relative
offers to teach her

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:15.149
ninth- and tenth-grade curricula

00:03:15.173 --> 00:03:17.399
during summer vacations.

00:03:17.966 --> 00:03:22.114
This is how she completed
her matriculation.

00:03:22.768 --> 00:03:26.156
The girl whom I am talking about to you

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:30.521
is me, Shameem,
who is talking before you now.

00:03:30.545 --> 00:03:36.982
(Applause)

00:03:37.006 --> 00:03:41.431
Throughout centuries, people
have been fighting for their identity.

00:03:41.768 --> 00:03:46.220
People have been loved, privileged,
because of their identity,

00:03:46.244 --> 00:03:48.666
their nationality, their ethnicity.

00:03:48.994 --> 00:03:52.704
Again, people have been hated, denied,

00:03:52.728 --> 00:03:56.164
because of their nationality,
their identity,

00:03:56.188 --> 00:03:58.922
their race, their gender, their religion.

00:04:00.791 --> 00:04:05.475
Identity determines your position
in society, wherever you live.

00:04:05.903 --> 00:04:10.684
So if you ask me, I would say
I hate this question of identity.

00:04:11.284 --> 00:04:17.069
Millions of girls in this world
are being denied their basic rights

00:04:17.093 --> 00:04:18.871
because of being female.

00:04:19.488 --> 00:04:25.542
I would have faced the same,
if I hadn't been raised as a boy.

00:04:26.204 --> 00:04:32.148
I was determined to continue my studies,
to learn, to be free.

00:04:32.998 --> 00:04:37.767
After my schooling, even enrolling
in college was not easy for me.

00:04:38.276 --> 00:04:41.181
I went on a three-day hunger strike.

00:04:41.205 --> 00:04:42.384
(Laughter)

00:04:42.408 --> 00:04:45.950
Then, I got permission for college.

00:04:45.974 --> 00:04:47.743
(Laughter)

00:04:47.767 --> 00:04:49.609
(Applause)

00:04:49.633 --> 00:04:53.327
In that way, I completed my college.

00:04:54.052 --> 00:04:58.990
Two years later, when the time came
for me to go to university,

00:04:59.014 --> 00:05:04.870
my father turned his eyes,
his attention, to my younger brothers.

00:05:04.894 --> 00:05:10.910
They need to be in school,
secure jobs and support the family.

00:05:10.934 --> 00:05:14.929
And as a woman, my place was to be home.

00:05:15.798 --> 00:05:17.442
But, I don't give up.

00:05:17.466 --> 00:05:22.482
I sign up for a two-year program
to become a lady health visitor.

00:05:22.506 --> 00:05:26.807
Then I hear about Thardeep
Rural Development Program,

00:05:26.831 --> 00:05:31.231
a non-profit organization
working to empower rural communities.

00:05:32.006 --> 00:05:33.156
I sneak away.

00:05:33.625 --> 00:05:38.337
I travel five hours
to interview for a position.

00:05:39.228 --> 00:05:44.109
It is the first time I am the farthest
from my home I have ever been.

00:05:44.133 --> 00:05:47.891
I am closest to my freedom
I have ever been.

00:05:48.323 --> 00:05:50.339
Luckily, I got the job,

00:05:50.363 --> 00:05:54.227
but the hardest part is facing my father.

00:05:54.251 --> 00:05:55.640
(Laughter)

00:05:56.522 --> 00:06:00.735
Relatives are already scaring him

00:06:00.759 --> 00:06:04.617
about his daughter wandering off,

00:06:04.641 --> 00:06:08.357
teasing him with talk
of his daughter crossing the border.

00:06:09.323 --> 00:06:11.178
When I return home,

00:06:11.202 --> 00:06:17.394
I want nothing more than just
to accept the position in Thardeep.

00:06:17.807 --> 00:06:22.712
So that night, I packed
all my things in a bag,

00:06:22.736 --> 00:06:27.428
and I walked into
my father's room and told him,

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:31.061
"Tomorrow morning,
the bus is going to come in.

00:06:31.085 --> 00:06:32.807
If you believe in me,

00:06:32.831 --> 00:06:34.896
if you believe in me,

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:40.457
you will wake me up
and take me to the bus station.

00:06:40.838 --> 00:06:43.220
If you don't, I'll understand."

00:06:43.244 --> 00:06:44.895
Then I went to sleep.

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:50.212
The next morning, my father
was standing beside me

00:06:50.236 --> 00:06:52.472
to take me to the bus stop.

00:06:52.496 --> 00:06:56.871
(Applause)

00:06:56.895 --> 00:07:00.960
That day, I understood
the importance of words.

00:07:01.379 --> 00:07:05.157
I understood how words affect our hearts,

00:07:05.855 --> 00:07:09.982
how words play
an important role in our lives.

00:07:10.371 --> 00:07:14.412
I understood words
are more powerful than fighting.

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:21.134
At TRDP, I saw there was a Pakistan
which I didn't know,

00:07:21.847 --> 00:07:26.218
a country much more complex
than I had realized.

00:07:26.242 --> 00:07:29.553
Until that, I thought
I had a difficult life.

00:07:29.577 --> 00:07:36.372
But here, I saw what women in other parts
of Pakistan were experiencing.

00:07:37.411 --> 00:07:39.124
It really opened my eyes.

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:43.958
Some women had 11 children
but nothing to feed them.

00:07:45.315 --> 00:07:50.484
For getting water, they would walk
three hours every day to wells.

00:07:51.593 --> 00:07:55.918
The nearest hospital was at least
32 kilometers away.

00:07:56.228 --> 00:07:58.601
So if a woman is in labor,

00:07:58.625 --> 00:08:01.853
she travels by camel
to get to the hospital.

00:08:03.061 --> 00:08:06.954
The distance is great;
she may die on her way.

00:08:07.934 --> 00:08:12.239
So now, this became
more than just a job for me.

00:08:12.847 --> 00:08:15.339
I discovered my power.

00:08:16.046 --> 00:08:18.260
Now, as I was getting salary,

00:08:18.284 --> 00:08:21.855
I started sending back money to my home.

00:08:21.879 --> 00:08:24.768
Relatives and neighbors
were noticing this.

00:08:24.792 --> 00:08:29.764
Now they started to understand
the importance of education.

00:08:30.345 --> 00:08:37.185
By that time, some other parents
started sending their daughters to school.

00:08:38.274 --> 00:08:42.371
Slowly, it became easier and acceptable

00:08:42.395 --> 00:08:45.163
for young women to be in college.

00:08:45.601 --> 00:08:51.859
Today, there isn't a single girl
out of school in my village.

00:08:51.883 --> 00:08:56.426
(Applause)

00:08:56.450 --> 00:09:01.232
Girls are doing jobs
in health sites, even in police.

00:09:01.847 --> 00:09:02.997
Life was good.

00:09:03.538 --> 00:09:05.620
But somewhere in my heart,

00:09:05.644 --> 00:09:11.664
I realized that my region,
beyond my village

00:09:11.688 --> 00:09:14.171
needs further change.

00:09:14.195 --> 00:09:18.204
This was also the time
when I joined Acumen Fellowship.

00:09:18.664 --> 00:09:23.283
There, I met leaders like me
across the country.

00:09:23.307 --> 00:09:27.078
And I saw they are taking
risks in their lives.

00:09:28.157 --> 00:09:32.307
I started to understand

00:09:32.331 --> 00:09:35.465
what leadership really means.

00:09:35.832 --> 00:09:39.308
So I decided to go back to my region

00:09:39.332 --> 00:09:43.382
and take a position as a teacher
in a remote school,

00:09:44.204 --> 00:09:48.490
a school that I have to reach by bus --

00:09:48.514 --> 00:09:53.235
two hours traveling,
every morning and evening.

00:09:53.768 --> 00:09:58.355
Though it was hard, on my first day I knew

00:09:58.379 --> 00:10:00.929
I made the right decision.

00:10:01.397 --> 00:10:04.418
The first day I walked into the school,

00:10:04.442 --> 00:10:08.806
I saw all these little Shameems
staring back at me --

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:10.163
(Laughter)

00:10:10.187 --> 00:10:12.903
with dreams in their eyes,

00:10:12.927 --> 00:10:16.635
the same dream of freedom
which I had in my childhood.

00:10:17.640 --> 00:10:21.973
So the girls are eager to learn,
but the school is understaffed.

00:10:22.771 --> 00:10:26.484
Girls sit hopeful,

00:10:26.508 --> 00:10:27.662
learn nothing,

00:10:27.686 --> 00:10:28.844
and they leave.

00:10:28.868 --> 00:10:31.670
I can't bear to see this happening.

00:10:31.694 --> 00:10:34.003
There was no turning back.

00:10:34.027 --> 00:10:36.876
I found my purpose.

00:10:37.734 --> 00:10:41.992
I enlisted a few of my friends
to help me to teach.

00:10:42.338 --> 00:10:46.608
I'm introducing my girls
to the outside world

00:10:46.632 --> 00:10:49.759
by extracurricular activities and books.

00:10:50.084 --> 00:10:54.379
I share with them the profiles
of the world's best leaders,

00:10:54.403 --> 00:10:57.926
like Martin Luther King
and Nelson Mandela.

00:10:58.466 --> 00:11:02.966
Last year, a few of our students
went to college.

00:11:03.657 --> 00:11:06.845
For me, I never stop studying.

00:11:07.228 --> 00:11:11.990
Today, I'm working to complete
my PhD in education --

00:11:12.014 --> 00:11:15.663
(Applause)

00:11:15.687 --> 00:11:20.855
which will allow me to gain
a management position

00:11:20.879 --> 00:11:22.410
in the school system,

00:11:22.434 --> 00:11:25.759
and I will be able to make more decisions

00:11:25.783 --> 00:11:29.774
and play a pivotal role in the system.

00:11:30.450 --> 00:11:33.997
I believe that without
educating the girls,

00:11:34.021 --> 00:11:36.665
we may not make world peace.

00:11:37.141 --> 00:11:40.340
We may not reduce child marriage.

00:11:40.364 --> 00:11:44.204
We may not reduce infant mortality rate.

00:11:44.228 --> 00:11:47.751
We may not reduce maternal mortality rate.

00:11:48.322 --> 00:11:52.220
For this, we have to continuously

00:11:52.244 --> 00:11:56.319
and collectively work together.

00:11:56.744 --> 00:11:59.196
At least I am playing my role,

00:11:59.220 --> 00:12:02.372
though the destination is not close.

00:12:03.046 --> 00:12:04.679
The road is not easy.

00:12:04.703 --> 00:12:07.420
But I have dreams in my eyes,

00:12:07.444 --> 00:12:12.029
and I am not going to look back now.

00:12:12.053 --> 00:12:13.220
Thank you.

00:12:13.244 --> 00:12:20.206
(Applause)

